  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy is equimolar WTaTiVZr, corresponding to approximately 20 at.% of each element.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equimolar WTaTiVZr forms a homogeneous, single-phase BCC solid solution.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11206460::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Incorporating Ta, Ti, V, and Zr into tungsten's BCC lattice creates substantial lattice distortion.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The lattice distortion lowers the barrier for edge-dislocation nucleation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The lattice distortion lowers the Peierls barrier for dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The reduced barrier causes plasticity to become dominated by edge dislocations.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced dislocation transmission and mobility promote more homogeneous plastic-strain distribution and relieve stress concentrations associated with crack initiation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified dislocation behavior produces effective crack blunting.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Commercially pure tungsten has limited slip systems and a higher barrier to dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The dislocation characteristics of pure tungsten cause it to tend toward brittle behavior at high temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 800–1200 °C, WTaTiVZr will have lower yield strength than commercially pure tungsten.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 800–1200 °C, WTaTiVZr will have significantly greater total plastic strain than commercially pure tungsten.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::webcard",
        "PMC5848905::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 800–1200 °C, WTaTiVZr will have greater fracture toughness than commercially pure tungsten.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "WTaTiVZr will delay crack initiation and propagation relative to commercially pure tungsten.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10213035::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed lattice-distortion mechanism dominates in high-temperature, dislocation-mediated plasma-facing-component deformation regimes.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
